{
  "note": "Put a picture behind the category title in the left column of every block on /pages/faq, with the accordions staying on the right. Malcolm's request, 2026-08-25: 'image with the title on top, image and title left and faq right'. IMAGES ARE PLACEHOLDERS - see configs/banners/page-faq-placeholders.json.",
  "why_injected_and_not_a_setting": "accordion-content has no image_picker anywhere in its schema, and its `content` field is a richtext whose Shopify sanitiser strips <img>. The two-column layout itself needed nothing - text_position already defaults to 'start', giving a 50/50 section-stack--horizontal. The left column was a title floating in 636px of empty space; this fills it.",
  "why_a_real_img_and_not_a_css_background": "A background-image would have been three lines, but it throws away alt text, native lazy-loading and the srcset. These are content images on a live store, so they are injected as real <img> elements with all three.",
  "two_variants_one_class_apart": "Shipped with the title OVER the picture. Adding .sg-faq-title-above to a section switches it to title ABOVE the picture. Both rule sets are in the stylesheet so they can be compared on the live page without another publish.",
  "template": "templates/page.faq.json",
  "images": [],
  "new_sections": [
    {
      "id": "faq_image_layout",
      "insert_after": "cta",
      "section": {
        "type": "custom-html",
        "settings": {
          "full_width": true,
          "remove_vertical_spacing": true,
          "remove_horizontal_spacing": true,
          "html": "<style>\n/* /pages/faq - picture + title in the left column, accordions right.\n   Claude Code, 2026-08-25, at Malcolm's request. PLACEHOLDER IMAGES.\n\n   The two-column layout is the theme's own: accordion-content defaults to\n   text_position 'start', which already gives .section-stack--horizontal with a 50%\n   .section-stack__intro on the left and .section-stack__main on the right. Nothing\n   about the columns is changed here - the left column was simply a title floating in\n   636px of empty space, and this fills it.\n\n   accordion-content has NO image setting in its schema, and its `content` field is a\n   richtext whose sanitiser strips <img>. So the picture is injected as a real <img>\n   at runtime rather than faked with a CSS background: that keeps alt text, native\n   lazy-loading and a srcset, which a background-image would all throw away.\n\n   Scoped to this page because the section lives in templates/page.faq.json. */\n\n.shopify-section--accordion-content .section-stack__intro .prose { position: relative; }\n\n.shopify-section--accordion-content .section-stack__intro .prose > img.sg-faq-image {\n  display: block;\n  width: 100%;\n  aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;\n  object-fit: cover;\n  border-radius: var(--rounded-sm);\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n/* Bottom scrim so the white title holds its contrast once REAL photographs replace\n   these flat placeholders. Measured on the homepage tiles earlier today: a flat\n   overlay strong enough for a 15px label greys the whole picture, whereas a bottom\n   gradient buys the contrast only where the type sits. Same reasoning, same shape. */\n.shopify-section--accordion-content .section-stack__intro .prose::after {\n  content: \"\";\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: auto 0 0 0;\n  height: 60%;\n  background: linear-gradient(to top,\n    rgb(0 0 0 / 0.62) 0%,\n    rgb(0 0 0 / 0.42) 24%,\n    rgb(0 0 0 / 0.14) 52%,\n    rgb(0 0 0 / 0) 100%);\n  border-radius: 0 0 var(--rounded-sm) var(--rounded-sm);\n  pointer-events: none;\n  z-index: 1;\n}\n\n.shopify-section--accordion-content .section-stack__intro .prose > h2 {\n  position: absolute;\n  z-index: 2;\n  left: var(--spacing-6, 1.5rem);\n  right: var(--spacing-6, 1.5rem);\n  bottom: var(--spacing-5, 1.25rem);\n  margin: 0;\n  color: #ffffff;\n}\n\n/* Variant, one class away: title ABOVE the picture rather than over it. Add\n   .sg-faq-title-above to the section to switch. Kept in the stylesheet so the two can\n   be compared on the live page without another publish. */\n.shopify-section--accordion-content.sg-faq-title-above .section-stack__intro .prose::after { display: none; }\n.shopify-section--accordion-content.sg-faq-title-above .section-stack__intro .prose > h2 {\n  position: static;\n  color: inherit;\n  margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-5, 1.25rem) 0;\n}\n.shopify-section--accordion-content.sg-faq-title-above .section-stack__intro .prose > img.sg-faq-image {\n  order: 2;\n}\n.shopify-section--accordion-content.sg-faq-title-above .section-stack__intro .prose {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n}\n</style>\n<script>\n/* Inject the FAQ category picture as the first child of each intro column.\n   Claude Code, 2026-08-25. PLACEHOLDERS - see the note in the stylesheet above.\n\n   Keyed on the section id suffix (the part after '__'), never on the full id: the\n   template-scoped prefix changes whenever the template is rebuilt. */\n(function () {\n  var IMAGES = {\n      \"faq_products\": {\n          \"src\": \"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0932/8679/3601/files/skingenetix-faq-placeholder-products-usage.jpg\",\n          \"alt\": \"Placeholder image - Skingenetix FAQ, Products & Usage\"\n      },\n      \"faq_ingredients\": {\n          \"src\": \"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0932/8679/3601/files/skingenetix-faq-placeholder-ingredients-safety.jpg\",\n          \"alt\": \"Placeholder image - Skingenetix FAQ, Ingredients & Safety\"\n      },\n      \"faq_shipping\": {\n          \"src\": \"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0932/8679/3601/files/skingenetix-faq-placeholder-orders-shipping.jpg\",\n          \"alt\": \"Placeholder image - Skingenetix FAQ, Orders & Shipping\"\n      },\n      \"faq_returns\": {\n          \"src\": \"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0932/8679/3601/files/skingenetix-faq-placeholder-returns-refunds.jpg\",\n          \"alt\": \"Placeholder image - Skingenetix FAQ, Returns & Refunds\"\n      },\n      \"faq_skincare\": {\n          \"src\": \"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0932/8679/3601/files/skingenetix-faq-placeholder-skincare-routine.jpg\",\n          \"alt\": \"Placeholder image - Skingenetix FAQ, Skincare & Routine\"\n      }\n  };\n  var WIDTHS = [400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200, 1600];\n\n  function init() {\n    document.querySelectorAll('.shopify-section--accordion-content').forEach(function (section) {\n      var key = (section.id || '').split('__').pop();\n      var spec = IMAGES[key];\n      if (!spec) return;\n\n      var prose = section.querySelector('.section-stack__intro .prose');\n      if (!prose || prose.querySelector('img.sg-faq-image')) return;\n\n      var img = document.createElement('img');\n      img.className = 'sg-faq-image';\n      img.src = spec.src + '?width=1200';\n      img.srcset = WIDTHS.map(function (w) {\n        return spec.src + '?width=' + w + ' ' + w + 'w';\n      }).join(', ');\n      // The intro column is 50% of the container, 636px at 1440.\n      img.sizes = '(max-width: 999px) 100vw, min(636px, 46vw)';\n      img.alt = spec.alt;\n      img.width = 1600;\n      img.height = 1200;\n      img.loading = 'lazy';\n      img.decoding = 'async';\n\n      prose.insertBefore(img, prose.firstChild);\n    });\n  }\n\n  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {\n    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);\n  } else {\n    init();\n  }\n})();\n</script>"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "the_422_trap": "Shopify rejects a custom-html `html` setting containing '{{', '}}', '{%' or '%}' - it reads them as Liquid. An inlined json.dumps() map ends '...}}' and trips it with no hint that JSON is the cause. Emit the map with indent so no two braces abut, and assert on all four tokens before pushing."
}
